<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Soloverse Rulebook Hub</title>
    <link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.webmanifest" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0f1015" />

    <!-- Pure, native PWA registration. No custom code download hooks to break on mobile webviews -->
    <script is:inline>
      if ('serviceWorker' in navigator) {
        window.addEventListener('load', () => {
          navigator.serviceWorker.register('/sw.js', { scope: '/' })
            .then(reg => console.log('PWA Registered:', reg.scope))
            .catch(err => console.error('PWA Failed:', err));
        });
      }
    </script>
</head>
<body>

    <!-- =============================================================== -->
    <div class="hub-logo-wrapper">
        <div class="image-container">
			<img
				src="/assets/images/layouts/soloverse-logo.png" 
				alt="Centred Image"
				loading="lazy"
			/>
		</div>
    </div>

    <header class="hero-center">

        <h1>Soloverse Rulebook Hub</h1>
            <p class="subtitle">
                <strong>What Are The Coloured Boxes?</strong> You'll notice that there are several Coloured Boxes below. 
                Please note that each Box represents part of the Soloverse, that is to say, different Games. 
                Soloverse allows you to focus on a Game Style that Suits Your Group the Most. 
                Here at Soloverse, however, we recommend beginning with [01-A] Crazy 8's [Tutorial] as that the Game Everyone knows. 
            </p>
            <p class="subtitle">
                -------
            </p>
            <p class="subtitle">
                Once a Game has been selected, You will find 2 specific Rulebook Types split across the Screen:
            </p>
            <p class="subtitle">
                <strong>On the Left:</strong> XX Soloverse - GAME NAME [Game Rulebook]. This Rulebook explains how to Play the Chosen Game.
            </p>
            <p class="subtitle">
                <strong>On the Right:</strong> XX Soloverse - GAME NAME [Definitions Rulebook]. This Rulebook explains what each Card in the Game does.
            </p>
            <p class="subtitle">
                Having these Rulebooks split side-by-side helps in quick referencing both the Game Rules and the Card Effects while You Learn the Basics, though generally You'll need the Card Definitions more than the Game Rules once You know how to Play. 
                And since my Card Rules are Digital, I am able to alter their Definitions, both allowing me to Balance them & allow Me to add more Game Modes over Time, expanding how much fun You can have in the Soloverse! 
                Also know that each additional Game that has been added to the Game, has kept the Card Definitions as close to the Originals in Crazy 8's as possible. 
            </p>
            <p class="subtitle">
                -------
            </p>
            <p class="subtitle">
                Finally, You'll also find a "VIEW OPTIONS" Button on the Top Right of each Rulebook Title. 
                This Button will allow you to choose a variety of Rulebook View Layouts, including:
            </p>
            <p class="subtitle">
                <strong>Standard: Game Rules and Card Rules</strong> This is the Default Layout, and is the most useful for referencing both the Game Rules and the Card Definitions while learning the Game Basics.
            </p>
            <p class="subtitle">
                <strong>Only Game Rules</strong> Just the Specific Game's Rules.
            </p>
            <p class="subtitle">
                <strong>Only Card Definitions</strong> Just the Specific Game's Card Definitions. You will mostly likely end up only needing this Rulebook after You've Learned the Game Rules.
            </p>

    </header>

<!-- ==================== PART 1: THE DYNAMIC GAME CARDS GRID ==================== -->
    <div class="grid">
        {renderedGames.map((game, index) => {
            // 1. Add all your light background hex codes to this list (lowercase or uppercase)
            const lightBoxes = ["#fff200", "#8cfffb", "#aded8f", "#b97a56"];
            
            // 2. Check if the current boxColor is one of the light colors
            const isLightBox = lightBoxes.includes(game.boxColor?.toLowerCase());

            // 3. Set your styles dynamically based on the check
            const titleColor = isLightBox ? "#111216" : "#ffffff";
            const textShadowRule = isLightBox ? "none" : "0 2px 4px rgba(0,0,0,0.6)";

            return (
                <button 
                    class="game-card selector-trigger" 
                    data-target={`vault-${game.id}`}
                    style="text-align: left; width: 100%; border: none; padding: 0; cursor: pointer; display: block; overflow: hidden;"
                >
                <div class="game-header" style={`background-color: ${game.boxColor}; border-bottom: 4px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.25);`}>
                    <h2 class="game-title" style={`color: ${titleColor}; text-shadow: ${textShadowRule}; margin-bottom: 4px;`}>
                        {game.title}
                    </h2>
    
                        {/* This line checks if a subtitle exists, and only renders it if it's not null */}
                        {game.subtitle && (
                            <p class="game-subtitle" style={`color: ${titleColor}; opacity: 0.85; font-size: 0.9em; margin: 0; text-shadow: ${textShadowRule};`}>
                                {game.subtitle}
                            </p>
                        )}
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="box-contents">
                        <p style="margin: 0; padding: 10px; color: #ced4da; font-size: 0.9rem;">
                            👉 Tap to open the live Rulebook and Card Database interface.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </button>
            );
        })}
    </div>

    <!-- ==================== NEW SPLIT-VIEW LIVE RULEBOOK PANELS ==================== -->
    <div class="vault-panels-holder" style="margin-top: 40px;">
        {finalizedGames.map((game, index) => {
            const Rules = game.RulesComponent;
            const Cards = game.CardsComponent;
            const Solo = game.SoloComponent;

            // Check metadata rules directly to see if Solo features are supported for this game card
            const hasSoloCapability = game.soloId !== null;

            return (
                <div 
                    id={`vault-${game.id}`} 
                    class={`game-panel ${index === 0 ? '' : 'hidden'}`} 
                    data-active-layout={game.initialLayout}
                >
                   <div class="panel-accent-header" style={`border-left: 6px solid ${game.boxColor}; background: #16171e; padding: 15px; border-radius: 4px; margin-bottom: 20px;`}>
                        <h2 style="margin: 0; color: #fff;">{game.title} - Operational Database</h2>
                    
                        {!game.isSingleColumnDefault && (
                            <div style="position: relative;" class="layout-menu-container">
                                <button class="theme-btn layout-trigger-btn" style="border-color: #3a3f54;">
                                    📋 View Options
                                </button>

                                {/* Stylized Dropdown Container matching your native rules layout cleanly */}
                                <div class="layout-dropdown rules-popup-box hidden">
                                    <div style="font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 700; color: #a4a6b5; margin-bottom: 8px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; padding-left: 4px;">
                                        Select Layout Matrix
                                    </div>
                                    <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px;">
                                        {Rules && Cards && (
                                            <button class="layout-opt-btn popup-item" data-view="rules-cards">
                                                Standard: Game + Cards
                                            </button>
                                        )}
                                        {hasSoloCapability && Cards && (
                                            <button class="layout-opt-btn popup-item" data-view="solo-cards">
                                                Solo Mode + Cards
                                            </button>
                                        )}
                                        {Rules && hasSoloCapability && (
                                            <button class="layout-opt-btn popup-item" data-view="rules-solo">
                                                Game + Solo Mode
                                            </button>
                                        )}
                                        {Rules && (
                                            <button class="layout-opt-btn popup-item" data-view="rules-only">
                                                Only Game Rules
                                            </button>
                                        )}
                                        {Cards && (
                                            <button class="layout-opt-btn popup-item" data-view="cards-only">
                                                Only Card Definitions
                                            </button>
                                        )}
                                        {hasSoloCapability && (
                                            <button class="layout-opt-btn popup-item" data-view="solo-only">
                                                Only Solo Mode
                                            </button>
                                        )}
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        )}
                    </div>

                    <div class={`split-view flex-layout-engine ${game.isSingleColumnDefault ? 'single-column' : ''}`}>
                        {Rules && (
                            <section class="content-block view-slot-rules">
                                <h3 style={`color: ${game.boxColor}; border-bottom: 1px solid #2a2d3d; padding-bottom: 10px;`}>📜 Game Rulebook</h3>
                                <div class="text-layer">
                                    <Rules />
                                </div>
                            </section>
                        )}

                        {Cards && (
                            <section class="content-block view-slot-cards">
                                <h3 style={`color: ${game.boxColor}; border-bottom: 1px solid #2a2d3d; padding-bottom: 10px;`}>🃏 Card Definitions & Reference</h3>
                                <div class="text-layer">
                                    <Cards />
                                </div>
                            </section>
                        )}

                        {hasSoloCapability && (
                            <section class="content-block view-slot-solo">
                                <h3 style={`color: ${game.boxColor}; border-bottom: 1px solid #2a2d3d; padding-bottom: 10px;`}>🕹️ Solo Mode Rules</h3>
                                <div class="text-layer">
                                    {Solo ? <Solo /> : <p style="color: #a4a6b5; font-style: italic;">Solo mode specification document compiled. Awaiting markdown layout initialization...</p>}
                                </div>
                            </section>
                        )}
                    </div>
                </div>
            );
        })}
    </div>

    <!-- ==================== PART 2: THE UPCOMING PIPELINE STACK ==================== -->
    <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
        <div class="section-divider">
            🛠️ In Development Blueprint Stack ({upcomingGames.length} Variants Pipeline)
        </div>

        <div class="grid">
            {upcomingGames.map((upcoming) => (
                <div class="blueprint-card">
                    <h2 class="blueprint-title">{upcoming.title}</h2>
                    <div class="status-badge">📦 Under Construction</div>
                </div>
            ))}
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ==================== PART 3: THE SMART HIGH-VISIBILITY PWA INSTALLATION OVERLAY ==================== -->
    <div id="pwa-banner" class="pwa-install-banner" style="display: none; position: fixed; top: 15px; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); width: 90%; max-width: 500px; z-index: 9999; background: #16171e; border: 2px solid #3b82f6; box-shadow: 0 15px 40px rgba(0,0,0,0.8); border-radius: 12px; flex-direction: column; padding: 15px;">
        <div class="pwa-header" style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 8px;">
            <div class="pwa-title" style="font-weight: 700; color: #fff; font-size: 1.05rem;">📱 Add Soloverse to Home Screen</div>
            <button id="pwa-close" class="pwa-close-btn" style="background: none; border: none; color: #a4a6b5; font-size: 1.5rem; cursor: pointer; line-height: 1;" aria-label="Close popup">×</button>
        </div>
        <div id="pwa-instructions" class="pwa-body" style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: #ced4da; line-height: 1.4; margin-bottom: 12px;">
            <!-- Content will be auto-generated by your script layer -->
        </div>
        <div class="pwa-action-row" style="display: flex; justify-content: flex-end; gap: 10px;">
            <button id="pwa-dismiss" class="theme-btn" style="padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 0.8rem; background: transparent; border-color: #2a2d3d;">Not Now</button>
            <button id="pwa-action-btn" class="theme-btn" style="padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 0.8rem; background: #3b82f6; color: #fff; border: none; display: none;">Install App</button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ==================== PART 3B: PLATFORM HOTFIX UPDATE CHANNEL NOTIFIER ==================== -->
    <div id="update-sync-banner" class="pwa-install-banner" style="display: none; position: fixed; top: 15px; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); width: 90%; max-width: 500px; z-index: 10000; background: #11121a; border: 2px solid #eab308; box-shadow: 0 15px 40px rgba(0,0,0,0.8); border-radius: 12px; flex-direction: column; padding: 15px;">
        <div class="pwa-header" style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 8px;">
            <div class="pwa-title" style="font-weight: 700; color: #eab308; font-size: 1.05rem;">⚡ Table Blueprint Changes Ready</div>
        </div>
        <div class="pwa-body" style="font-size: 0.88rem; color: #ced4da; line-height: 1.4; margin-bottom: 12px;">
            New game balancing mechanics, variations, or card layout optimizations have been updated on the live server environment.
        </div>
        <div class="pwa-action-row" style="display: flex; justify-content: flex-end;">
            <button id="update-sync-action-btn" class="theme-btn" style="padding: 8px 16px; font-size: 0.85rem; background: #eab308; color: #111216; border: none;">Sync Assets Offline</button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ==================== SOLOVERSE VAULT CENTRAL STYLING ENGINE ==================== -->
    <style is:inline>
        .hero-center {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            align-items: center; /* Centers items horizontally */
            text-align: center;  /* Centers inline multi-line text */
            gap: 10px;           /* Adds clean spacing between h1 and p */
            margin: 40px auto;   /* Generates balance margin space around block */
        }
  
        :root, [data-theme="dark"] {
            --bg-main: #0f1015;
            --bg-card: #16171e;
            --bg-main-box: #1c1e27;
            --text-primary: #e4e6eb;
            --text-muted: #a4a6b5;
            --text-body: #ced4da;
            --text-divider: #2a2d3d;
            --color-link: #3b82f6;
        }

        body { 
            background-color: var(--bg-main); 
            color: var(--text-primary); 
            font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; 
            margin: 0; 
            padding: 20px; 
            max-width: 100vw;
            overflow-x: hidden;
        }
        
        .vault-container { 
            max-width: 1400px; 
            margin: 0 auto; 
            width: 100%;
        }

        header { 
            text-align: center; 
            margin-bottom: 40px; 
            border-bottom: 1px solid #2a2d3d; 
            padding-bottom: 25px; 
        }

        /* 2. DYNAMIC SELECTION CARDS GRID PROFILE */
        .grid { 
            display: grid; 
            grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(280px, 1fr)); 
            gap: 20px; 
            width: 100%; 
            margin-bottom: 40px;
        }

        .game-card {
            background: #16171e;
            border-radius: 16px; 
            overflow: hidden;    
            border: 1px solid #2d3139; 
            box-shadow: 0 10px 25px -5px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
            transition: transform 0.2s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1), box-shadow 0.2s ease;
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
        }
        .game-card:hover {
            transform: translateY(-4px);
            box-shadow: 0 20px 25px -5px rgba(0,0,0,0.6);
        }

        .game-header {
            padding: 24px 20px;
            text-align: center;
            position: relative; 
            /* 🚀 THE ZOOM FIX: Pre-rounds the inner color block so fractional scaling remainders can't bleed out */
            border-top-left-radius: 14px;
            border-top-right-radius: 14px;
            background-clip: padding-box; /* Forces the background color to respect inner boundary layers */
        }
        .game-header::after {
            content: '';
            position: absolute;
            inset: 0;
            background: linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12), rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35));
            pointer-events: none; 
        }

        .game-title {
            position: relative;
            z-index: 10; 
            margin: 0;
            font-size: 1.15rem;
            font-weight: 800;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 0.03em;
        }

        .box-contents {
            padding: 20px;
            background: #1c1e27; 
            flex-grow: 1;
        }

        /* 3. SPLIT-VIEW OPERATIONS INTERFACE DASHBOARD */
        .vault-panels-holder { width: 100%; }
        .game-panel { 
            animation: vaultFadeIn 0.35s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1); 
            width: 100%;
        }
        .hidden { display: none !important; }

        /* ==========================================================================
           3. SPLIT-VIEW OPERATIONS INTERFACE DASHBOARD (RE-CENTERED & VIEWPORT-LOCKED)
           ========================================================================= */
        .vault-panels-holder { 
            width: 100%; 
            max-width: 1400px;
            margin: 40px auto 0 auto; /* Perfectly re-centers the core panel layout tray */
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }
        
        .game-panel { 
            animation: vaultFadeIn 0.35s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1); 
            width: 100%;
        }
        
        .hidden { 
            display: none !important; 
        }

        /* 📱 DEFAULT PORTRAIT VIEWPORT SETTING */
        .split-view.flex-layout-engine { 
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            gap: 20px; 
            margin-top: 20px; 
            width: 100%;
            height: 75vh; /* Sets a locked canvas container for scrolling columns */
        }

        /* 🕹️ LOCKED MULTI-SCROLL INDEPENDENT COLUMNS (ONLY active for multi-doc layouts) */
        .split-view.flex-layout-engine .content-block { 
            background: #16171e; 
            border: 1px solid #2a2d3d; 
            padding: 20px; 
            border-radius: 8px; 
            min-width: 0; 
            display: none; /* Controlled dynamically by data-active-layout attributes */
            flex-direction: column;
            flex: 1;
            overflow-y: auto; 
            -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch; 
            box-shadow: inset 0 0 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);
        }

        /* 🎮 AUTOMATIC LANDSCAPE BREAKPOINT FOR SIDE-BY-SIDE SIDE PANEL GRID ENGINE */
        @media screen and (min-width: 600px) and (orientation: landscape) { 
            .split-view.flex-layout-engine:not(.single-column) { 
                display: grid !important;
                grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; /* Splits the view perfectly 50/50 */
                gap: 25px;
